{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791703686,"nonce":"riNaHeKOQi910N9JdAHmorUHxrU=","title":"A host's canvas element cannot be drawn","message":"The renderer draws canvases by slot (node.setResource(slot, true) and renderer.registerCanvas), but a host app had no way to reach either: Host.mount dropped the renderer its window made, and nothing gave a canvas element a slot. The tag was in builtinTags and drew nothing.\n\nAdded host.canvases (src/native/canvases.ts): draw(canvas, drawing) gives the element a slot and registers it with every renderer drawing the host; a drawing's prepare(renderer, scope) makes its pipelines and resources once per renderer and returns the paint, released with the scope when the canvas stops, is destroyed, or the renderer is detached. Host.mount attaches its window's renderer; attach(renderer) does it for one made by hand. requestFrame() lets an animating canvas ask for the next frame from its paint. SceneRenderer gained a device getter for the resources a drawing makes.\n\nTests: tests/native-canvas-element.mjs (drawn in place with the probe shader, clipped at its rounded corner, a second renderer, detach releases, stop, destroy with a parent, only a canvas). Mutations caught: no slot set (nothing drawn); no forget on destroy (not released). The wiki's GPU canvas page draws an animated WGSL shader resolved with TypeGPU at run time; adapters/test/wiki.mjs checks it draws, asks for frames while playing, and holds when paused.","files":null}]}